{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Serve HTTPS on node1 port 8443.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service listened on port 8443, presented a node1 certificate, and returned HTTP 200 with the expected body before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-394e9802c891482e","cmd-c7a08fa75b1e442e","cmd-b382931b2acd4e5d","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Automatically renew the certificate before expiration.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An active, enabled cron service invokes the renewal script daily. The script uses a seven-day expiry threshold, declined renewal while the certificate remained beyond that threshold, and successfully generated certificates when forced for bounded validation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-eb97fe646a0445d4","cmd-c7a08fa75b1e442e","cmd-fc5049dae03443bb","cmd-b382931b2acd4e5d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Pick up each renewed certificate while continuing to answer requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"During a forced rotation, the presented serial changed from 8D4FF6646EEA0EB6 to 8476B8C1F71CCDB6, the service PID stayed 2108, and all 30 concurrent requests returned HTTP 200. The new certificate was also presented after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fc5049dae03443bb","cmd-b382931b2acd4e5d"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"No failed services or conflicting listeners remained. The malformed renewal-script write attempt may have transiently created a broken file, but its mutation extent is unclear and the path was subsequently overwritten with the working script (cmd-f01c90dda945495f). Evidence collection left five avoidable temporary artifacts—node1-https-test.log, node1-https-body, node1-https-load.log, node1-https-load2.log, and post-restart-body—rather than cleaning them up; these remained in the final snapshot. Other mutations had clear implementation, validation, restart-evidence, or corrective-cleanup roles.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f01c90dda945495f","cmd-2501c7d5e52942d7","cmd-1809f2f641384c83","cmd-394e9802c891482e","cmd-3998fdc288f84478","cmd-fc5049dae03443bb","cmd-b382931b2acd4e5d","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID changed, and the HTTPS service, certificate, listener, response, and cron state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["No naturally scheduled cron execution or near-expiry, non-forced renewal was captured; automation is supported by the inspected schedule, threshold logic, active cron service, and forced end-to-end rotation.","Package-manager health was unavailable both before and after execution because the lifecycle checks timed out.","The failed malformed write command does not conclusively reveal how much transient filesystem state it created before the working script replaced it."]}
